JUJU:



; Philosophy:
Hex console utility:  hex
It's a customized experience that is meant for production quality workflows, but
also for educating on the importance of maintaining console workflows in average
day to day computing lives.

; Why use Hex, instead of just Bash and Shell?
Well, you can screw up more easily in a typical console and Hex is just a more c
ustomized console utility workspace, meant to work with Shell and by editing Hex
's Pascal sources.

It's as much of a mental model for you to latch onto, as it is about the tooling
itself.

Custom solutions that have been studied and emerge naturally, are usually better
than what you get marketed, on most of the internet, so my millionaire wife pays
me, to maintain The Juju ecosystem, so that i can keep balling like this. I also
support a lot of other work, through it. I only enjoy life, through the finest o
f interfaces, that work. For some those are other people's faces, for some, they
are console applications, that console them deep into the night, when nothing el
se outside goes according to plan and when people gravitate towards the void, by
staring into the gaping abyss that is their future, not formative of our present
worries, in the slightest.


Life's works,
The First Philosophers
;;



